      "zh": "于是扫罗不追赶大卫，回去攻打非利士人。因此那地方名叫西拉・哈玛希罗结。",
      "en": "So Saul stopped pursuing David and went to confront the Philistines. Therefore that place is called Sela Hammahlekoth.[NOTE:1]",
      "notes": [
        "The name סֶלַע הַמַּחְלְקוֹת (selaʿ hammakhleqot) probably means “Rock of Divisions” in Hebrew, in the sense that Saul and David parted company there (cf. NAB “Gorge of Divisions”; TEV “Separation Hill”). This etymology assumes that the word derives from the Hebrew root II חָלַק (khalaq, “to divide”; HALOT 322 s.v. II חלק). However, there is another root I חלק, which means “to be smooth or slippery” (HALOT 322 s.v. I חלק). If the word is taken from this root, the expression would mean “Slippery Rock.”"
      ],
